Lumen Labs Q3 2026 Business Review. Revenue for Q3 was 14.2 million euros, up 18 percent from Q3 2025, when revenue was 12.0 million euros. Recurring subscriptions made up 81 percent of revenue. The company ended the quarter with 1,240 paying customers, which is 96 more than at the end of Q2.
---page---
Customer retention. Monthly churn decreased from 3.8 percent in Q2 to 3.1 percent in Q3. The decline was attributed to the redesigned onboarding flow that launched in July. Net revenue retention was 109 percent. The largest remaining churn driver was price sensitivity among small accounts with fewer than 10 seats.
---page---
Regions and people. EMEA contributed 52 percent of revenue, North America 33 percent and APAC 15 percent. The Singapore office opened in August with 12 employees. Total headcount at the end of the quarter was 218. The main priority for Q4 is the launch of the Analytics Pro tier on 3 November.
